## Rubric
- [x] Confirm `SpecificEtag::new` can represent a wildcard after accepting a quoted HTTP entity tag (`"*"`) even though raw `*` is rejected.
- [x] Confirm the HTTP write-condition parser rejects unquoted `If-Match: *` but accepts quoted `If-Match: "*"` and returns `WriteCondition::IfMatch`.
- [x] Confirm write precondition evaluation passes the stored specific ETag string into the generic matcher that special-cases bare `*` as wildcard.
- [x] Dynamically demonstrate that `IfMatch("*")` succeeds against an existing object with a different ETag, while still failing for absent objects, proving wildcard-over-existing-object behavior.
