## Report
Validated the finding. The vulnerable flow is present in the checked-out commit baf862538dea2feed097d67a3d65fc8c93afd83d: `SpecificEtag::new` rejects only raw `*` before quote stripping, then stores `"*"` as bare `*` (`crates/server-core/src/conditional.rs:40-49`). The HTTP write parser rejects only unquoted `If-Match: *` (`crates/server-http/src/http/conditional.rs:33-41`) and then calls `SpecificEtag::new` for other If-Match values (`crates/server-http/src/http/conditional.rs:59-62`). The write checker passes `required_etag.as_str()` into `etags_match` (`crates/server-core/src/conditional.rs:274-278`), and `etags_match` treats bare `*` as wildcard (`crates/server-core/src/conditional.rs:182-185`).

I added targeted PoC integration tests. The core PoC asserts raw `*` is rejected, quoted `"*"` is accepted and stored as `*`, and `check_write_conditions(IfMatch("*"), Some("definitely-different-etag"))` succeeds (`crates/server-core/tests/poc_quoted_star.rs:4-21`). The HTTP PoC constructs an `S3Request` with `if-match: "*"`, confirms raw `*` is rejected, confirms quoted-star parses to `WriteCondition::IfMatch` with `etag.as_str() == "*"`, then confirms it matches an existing different ETag (`crates/server-http/tests/poc_quoted_star_http.rs:18-31`). Both tests passed: `test quoted_star_specific_etag_becomes_wildcard_for_write_if_match ... ok` and `test http_if_match_quoted_star_is_accepted_then_matches_any_existing_etag ... ok`.

Crash attempt: this is a logic/integrity bug, not a memory-safety bug; the targeted debug test binary executed successfully and did not crash. Valgrind attempt: `valgrind not installed`. GDB attempt through `rust-gdb` failed because `gdb` is not installed. I used LLDB successfully. The LLDB breakpoint at `crates/server-core/src/conditional.rs:277` stopped inside `check_write_conditions`; `frame variable --depth 8 *required_etag` showed the internal pointer value was `"*"`, while `obj_etag` was the different string `abcdef1234567890`, and the test then continued to `ok`. This confirms the accepted quoted-star If-Match reaches the wildcard-sensitive write-condition matcher and succeeds against a nonmatching existing ETag.

